# Code Style

Prettier + ESLint enforced. Run `yarn prettier` and `yarn lint`. Generate code that satisfies `@furystack/eslint-plugin` from the start — don't rely on the linter to catch violations.

## Naming

| Kind | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| File | kebab-case `.ts` / `.tsx` | `session.ts`, `service-table.tsx` |
| Spec | co-located, `.spec.ts` / `.spec.tsx` | `session.spec.ts` |
| E2E spec | `e2e/<flow>.spec.ts` | `e2e/login.spec.ts` |
| Class / type / component / service token | PascalCase | `ProcessManager`, `StackCraftApi` |
| Function / variable | camelCase, verb-led | `getCurrentUser`, `validateEmail` |
| Constant | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE | `MAX_RETRY_COUNT` |
| Boolean | `is*` / `has*` / `should*` / `can*` prefix | `isAuthenticated` |
| Event handler (internal) | `handle*` | `handleSubmit` |
| Event prop callback | `on*` | `onSave` |
| Type alias | prefer `type` over `interface`. No `I` prefix, no `Type` suffix | `type User = { ... }` |
| Component props | PascalCase + `Props` suffix | `type ServiceTableProps` |
| Shade element name | kebab-case, unique, namespaced | `customElementName: 'sc-service-table'` |

## Imports

Order, blank line between groups:

1. Node built-ins
2. External deps
3. `@furystack/*` packages
4. Workspace packages (`common`)
5. Relative imports
6. Type-only imports last in each group

```typescript
import { join } from 'path'

import { defineService } from '@furystack/inject'
import { Shade } from '@furystack/shades'

import type { Service } from 'common'

import { ProcessManager } from '../services/process-manager.js'
import type { ServiceTableProps } from './types.js'
```

Group same-package imports together. Sort alphabetically when many.

## Workspace layout

```
stack-craft/
├── common/                                # shared types + per-module API contracts
│   └── src/
│       ├── apis/<module>.ts               # one RestApi-derived interface per module
│       └── apis/index.ts                  # re-export
├── frontend/                              # Shades app
│   └── src/
│       ├── components/<x>.tsx
│       ├── components/<x>/index.tsx + assets
│       ├── pages/<x>.tsx                  # route targets
│       └── services/<x>.ts                # frontend services (defineService)
├── service/                               # REST backend
│   └── src/
│       ├── service.ts                     # entry — composes per-module setup
│       ├── config.ts                      # injector configuration
│       ├── app-models/<module>/
│       │   ├── setup-<module>-rest-api.ts # per-module endpoint registration
│       │   └── setup-<module>-store.ts    # per-module store / DataSet wiring
│       ├── services/                      # singleton service tokens
│       └── setup-entity-sync.ts
├── monaco-mfe/                            # Monaco editor MFE
└── e2e/                                   # Playwright specs
```

`common` re-exports everything through `common/src/index.ts` (with `apis/index.ts` aggregating per-module types). Use `.js` import suffix on relative paths (NodeNext ESM).

## File structure

```typescript
// 1. imports
import { defineService } from '@furystack/inject'

// 2. types
type SessionState = 'initializing' | 'unauthenticated' | 'authenticated'

// 3. constants
const DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS = 5000

// 4. helpers
const formatError = (err: unknown): string =>
  err instanceof Error ? err.message : 'Unknown error'

// 5. main export
export const SessionService = defineService({
  name: 'app/SessionService',
  lifetime: 'singleton',
  factory: ({ inject, onDispose }) => { /* ... */ },
})
```

## Service / component structure

Component render order: services → host props → refs → observable subscriptions → local state → handlers → JSX.

```typescript
export const ServiceRow = Shade<ServiceRowProps>({
  customElementName: 'sc-service-row',
  render: ({ props, injector, useObservable, useState }) => {
    const pm = injector.get(ProcessManager)
    const [status] = useObservable('status', pm.getStatus(props.serviceId))
    const [isExpanded, setIsExpanded] = useState('expanded', false)

    const handleToggle = () => setIsExpanded(!isExpanded)

    return <div>{/* ... */}</div>
  },
})
```

## JSX

Multi-line for >2 attrs. Single-line for trivial cases. No nested ternaries — use early returns for >2 branches.

```tsx
// ✅
<button type="button" onclick={handleClick} style={{ padding: '8px' }}>
  Save
</button>

// ❌ nested ternary
{isLoading ? <Loading /> : error ? <Err /> : <Content />}
```

## JSDoc

Required on exported services / components / endpoints. Include `@example` when usage isn't obvious.

## Comments

Only for non-obvious intent / trade-offs / constraints. Never narrate what code does.

```typescript
// ✅
// Exponential backoff: 1s, 2s, 4s, 8s, capped at 30s
const delay = Math.min(1000 * 2 ** attempt, 30000)

// ❌
// Set count to 0
const count = 0
```
